<title>POLAND: Poland's Gdansk refinery lowers diesel prices.</title>
<headline>Poland's Gdansk refinery lowers diesel prices.</headline>
<dateline>GDANSK, Poland 1997-04-03</dateline>
<text>
<p>Poland's second largest refinery,  Rafineria Gdanska SA, will on Friday lower the price of diesel fuel by 30 zlotys per tonne, which translates into a three grosz per litre savings, its president said.</p>
<p>&quot;Starting tomorrow Rafineria Gdanska will lower its wholesale price of diesel by 30 zlotys per tonne,&quot; Wlodzimierz Dyrka told a news conference on Thursday.</p>
<p>Last month the Gdansk refinery cut its diesel price by one grosz per litre while increasing petrol prices by about three groszes per liter.</p>
<p>The refinery owns 16 petrol stations and has 60 stations with which it has a distribution contract.</p>
<p>-- Ryszard Wesolowski +48 22 653 9700</p>
